From: Daniel <daniel@matv.io>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: imx371: disable PDAF raw-pixel output to restore front-camera colour

The IMX371 front sensor on the OnePlus 6T (SDM845) produces grayscale
selfies: all Bayer channels in captured frames read R≈G≈B, effectively
reducing every pixel to luminance. The root cause was identified by
comparing the imx371.c sensor mode register table against the
imx376.c rear-sensor driver in the same tree, which is known to produce
correct colour output.

Four registers differ between the two drivers and are responsible for the
monochrome output:

  0x3F14 (PRIMARY): PDAF raw-pixel output enable.
    imx371.c = 0x01 (enabled — the direct cause of R≈G≈B; with PDAF
    raw-pixel mode active the ISP receives phase-detect/luminance data on
    all colour channels instead of a normal Bayer mosaic).
    imx376.c = 0x00 (disabled — normal colour Bayer output).

  0x3F3C: PDAF companion / raw-pixel mode select.
    imx371.c = 0x01, imx376.c = 0x00.

  0x3E20: Pixel output type select.
    imx371.c = 0x00, imx376.c = 0x03.

  0xBC41: Sensor output format companion.
    imx371.c = 0x01, imx376.c = 0x03.

This patch mirrors the imx376 known-good values for all four registers,
disabling the PDAF raw-pixel output path and restoring normal Bayer colour
readout from the IMX371 front sensor.

Note: the register semantics above are inferred from driver-differential
analysis — there is no public IMX371 datasheet available for verification.
See the investigation report at ~/fajita-notes/camera-project/front-mono-investigation.md
for the full differential comparison, including additional registers that
differ between imx371.c and imx376.c (0x3F4C, 0x3F4D, 0x3F78, 0x3F79)
which were left unchanged in this patch but may need to be mirrored too if
colour is not fully restored after testing this change.

This patch is UNVERIFIED — it requires an on-device kernel reflash to test.
Do NOT apply without that test. Kernel source: rev c4804e960aef,
tag sdm845-6.16.7-r0.

---
 drivers/media/i2c/imx371.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/media/i2c/imx371.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/imx371.c
@@ -358,7 +358,7 @@
 	{CCI_REG8(0x040D), 0x30},
 	{CCI_REG8(0x040E), 0x0D},
 	{CCI_REG8(0x040F), 0x80},
-	{CCI_REG8(0xBC41), 0x01},
+	{CCI_REG8(0xBC41), 0x03},
 	{CCI_REG8(0x034C), 0x12},
 	{CCI_REG8(0x034D), 0x30},
 	{CCI_REG8(0x034E), 0x0D},
@@ -377,7 +377,7 @@
 	{CCI_REG8(0x0821), 0x70},
 	{CCI_REG8(0x0822), 0x00},
 	{CCI_REG8(0x0823), 0x00},
-	{CCI_REG8(0x3E20), 0x00},
+	{CCI_REG8(0x3E20), 0x03},
 	{CCI_REG8(0x3E37), 0x00},
 	{CCI_REG8(0x3E3B), 0x00},
 	{CCI_REG8(0x3614), 0x00},
@@ -397,9 +397,9 @@
 	{CCI_REG8(0x3C05), 0x14},
 	{CCI_REG8(0x3C06), 0x01},
 	{CCI_REG8(0x3C07), 0x01},
-	{CCI_REG8(0x3F14), 0x01},
+	{CCI_REG8(0x3F14), 0x00},
 	{CCI_REG8(0x3F17), 0x00},
-	{CCI_REG8(0x3F3C), 0x01},
+	{CCI_REG8(0x3F3C), 0x00},
 	{CCI_REG8(0x3F78), 0x00},
 	{CCI_REG8(0x3F79), 0xB4},
 	{CCI_REG8(0x3F7C), 0x00},
